      "title": "As Japan’s yen peaks, is the era of budget-friendly trips coming to an end for Australian travellers?",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/14/as-japans-yen-peaks-is-the-era-of-budget-friendly-trips-coming-to-an-end-for-australian-travellers",
      "description": "<p>The currency has now reached its highest level against the US and Australian dollars in six months</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>In the unpredictable world of global currency markets, there has been one safe bet: that the Japanese yen would continue its relentless decline.</p><p>In recent weeks, that trade has started to unravel after Tokyo and Washington intervened to support the longsuffering Japanese currency.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/14/as-japans-yen-peaks-is-the-era-of-budget-friendly-trips-coming-to-an-end-for-australian-travellers\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-13T15:00:09"
    },
