      "title": "Crossbench MPs launch push to stop Australian military exports being used in human rights breaches",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/14/crossbench-mps-launch-push-to-stop-australian-military-exports-being-used-in-human-rights-breaches",
      "description": "<p>‘Red lines’ legislation would forbid defence equipment technology or services being used, includes parts for F-35 fighter jets</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Crossbench MPs including David Pocock and Sophie Scamps will put pressure on the Albanese government to ban Australian goods from being used by the Israeli military – <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/science/2025/nov/22/human-rights-fears-over-australias-role-in-f-35-parts-after-trumps-decision-to-sell-fighter-jets-to-saudi-arabia\">including for F-35 fighter jets</a> – by introducing a bill designed to force it to adhere to international obligations.</p><p>The group’s “red lines” legislation, to be presented on Monday, would outlaw defence equipment, technology or services being used where they could breach Australia’s international human rights obligations.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/14/crossbench-mps-launch-push-to-stop-australian-military-exports-being-used-in-human-rights-breaches\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-13T15:00:09"
    },
    {
      "title": "Pauline Hanson and Barnaby Joyce stayed at Gina Rinehart’s $20m mansion after One Nation fundraisers",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/14/pauline-hanson-and-barnaby-joyce-stayed-at-gina-rinehart-brisbane-mansion-after-one-nation-fundraisers-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p><strong>Exclusive:</strong> New details underscoring depth of relationship between billionaire and party revealed in first episode of Guardian podcast The Populist</p><ul><li><p>Listen to the Guardian’s podcast <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/series/guardian-australia-podcast-series\">The Populist here</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Pauline Hanson and Barnaby Joyce stayed overnight at Gina Rinehart’s $20m Brisbane mansion after fundraising events held for One Nation, Guardian Australia can reveal.</p><p>On one occasion, Joyce conducted a live television interview with Channel Seven’s Sunrise program from a room that appears to be a bedroom in Rinehart’s home.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/14/pauline-hanson-and-barnaby-joyce-stayed-at-gina-rinehart-brisbane-mansion-after-one-nation-fundraisers-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-13T15:00:07"
