      "title": "First H5 bird flu death of endangered Australian sea lion recorded amid fears for small population",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/13/first-h5-bird-flu-death-of-endangered-australian-sea-lion-kangaroo-island",
      "description": "<p>South Australian authorities say case discovered on Kangaroo Island is first for species of which less than 12,000 animals remain</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>South Australia has recorded the first death of an endangered Australian sea lion from H5 bird flu.</p><p>Experts say <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/25/australia-has-just-12000-sea-lions-left-and-carnage-may-await-them-as-bird-flu-takes-hold-scientists-warn\">about 12,000 Australian sea lions remain</a> – though a more recent estimate put the figure at less than 10,000. Most of the population are found in South Australia, with the remainder in Western Australia.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/13/first-h5-bird-flu-death-of-endangered-australian-sea-lion-kangaroo-island\">Continue reading...</a>",
